WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.630
A coral reef looks like rock.

2
00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:04.987
But it is built by tiny animals,

3
00:00:04.987 --> 00:00:07.042
and they share their homes with even

4
00:00:07.042 --> 00:00:08.398
tinier plants.

5
00:00:08.798 --> 00:00:11.248
Each coral polyp hosts algae inside its

6
00:00:11.248 --> 00:00:12.142
tissue.

7
00:00:12.142 --> 00:00:14.255
The algae make food from sunlight,

8
00:00:14.255 --> 00:00:15.543
and give the coral most of its

9
00:00:15.543 --> 00:00:16.482
colour.

10
00:00:16.882 --> 00:00:18.763
It's a good deal for both.

11
00:00:18.763 --> 00:00:20.365
The algae can supply up to ninety

12
00:00:20.365 --> 00:00:22.383
per cent of the coral's energy.

13
00:00:22.784 --> 00:00:24.514
But if the water stays too warm

14
00:00:24.514 --> 00:00:26.673
for weeks, even a degree above the

15
00:00:26.673 --> 00:00:28.136
usual summer peak,

16
00:00:28.136 --> 00:00:29.947
the coral is stressed.

17
00:00:29.947 --> 00:00:31.375
It pushes the algae out,

18
00:00:31.375 --> 00:00:33.579
and its white skeleton shows through.

19
00:00:33.979 --> 00:00:36.080
A bleached coral is not dead yet.

20
00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:37.427
If the water cools in time,

21
00:00:37.427 --> 00:00:38.890
the algae can return.

22
00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:40.167
If the heat lasts,

23
00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:41.617
the coral starves.

24
00:00:42.016 --> 00:00:45.429
India has reefs in four places:

25
00:00:45.429 --> 00:00:46.706
the Gulf of Mannar,

26
00:00:46.706 --> 00:00:48.309
the Gulf of Kachchh,

27
00:00:48.309 --> 00:00:53.347
Lakshadweep, and the Andaman and Nicobar Islands.

28
00:00:53.347 --> 00:00:55.066
In twenty twenty-four,

29
00:00:55.066 --> 00:00:58.895
NOAA confirmed the fourth global bleaching event.

30
00:00:59.296 --> 00:01:01.583
For Prelims: bleaching is the loss of

31
00:01:01.583 --> 00:01:03.882
algae, caused mainly by heat,

32
00:01:03.882 --> 00:01:05.380
and it can be reversed if the

33
00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:06.934
sea cools in time.

